  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What is the radius of the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+6y+(z-1)^{2}=16?$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+6y+(z-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}+6y+9)+(z-1)^{2} & =16+9 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2}={5}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $5.$",
